     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Hayden Group Clinic\nPatient: Gabriella Lee DOB: 03/09/1959 Sex: F MRN: 239948\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-08-17 Epilepsy / seizure disorder BP 139/94 Wt 164\n 2025-03-11 Annual physical BP 144/87 Wt 160\n 2024-10-02 Epilepsy / seizure disorder BP 145/89 Wt 152\n 2024-04-26 Medication refill BP 135/86 Wt 2023-11-18 Epilepsy / seizure disorder BP 142/95 Wt 159\n 2023-06-12 Lab review BP 138/88 Wt 150\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Epilepsy / seizure disorder (seizure-free for 12 years) - currently controlled with topiramate 100 mg daily\n • Blood pressure within normal limits on all visits\n • Weight within normal limits on all visits\n • Social history: alcohol intake approximately 3 drinks per week\n • No documented history of tobacco use\n\nAdditional Findings:\n • Comprehensive lab results from Heritage Diagnostic Services on 12/05/11 indicate:\n - Total cholesterol: 310 mg/dL\n - HDL cholesterol: 67 mg/dL\n - Fructosamine: 279 micromol/L\n - Nicotine metabolite: Negative\n - Gamma GT: 44 U/L\n\nReview of Systems:\n • Cardiovascular: No chest pain, palpitations, or edema\n • Respiratory: No shortness of breath, wheezing, or cough\n • Gastrointestinal: No abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, or changes in bowel habits\n • Neurological: No headaches, dizziness, or changes in vision\n\nPhysical Examination:\n • General: Alert and oriented, no acute distress\n • Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops\n • Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes or crackles\n • Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly\n • Neurological: Cranial nerves II-XII intact, motor and sensory intact, reflexes 2+ and symmetric, no focal deficits\n\nImpression:\nGabriella Lee is a 66-year-old female with a well-documented history of epilepsy, has been effectively managed with topiramate 100 mg daily. She has remained seizure-free for the past 12 years. Her recent visits have shown stable vital signs and weight, and her comprehensive lab work from 12/05/11 indicates controlled cholesterol levels with an HDL of 67 mg/dL and a fructosamine level of 279 micromol/L. There are no signs of nicotine use. Her family history includes breast cancer in her mother, who was diagnosed at 44 and passed away at 53, and a history of stroke in her father who passed away at 51. Additionally, her mother suffered from a myocardial infarction at 74, but the outcome is unknown.\n\nPlan:\n • Continue topiramate 100 mg daily for epilepsy management\n • Routine follow-up for ongoing monitoring of seizure control and medica"
